      "raw_block_sha256": "630138d61674716bf8030144c0a1a631f965d72e05cc8c4920fa0c804313cd57",
      "operative_body": "That Council: Approve the following funding applications for the year 2018: 1. Historically Funded Requests: a) Vancouver Island South Film and Media Commission - $2,000 to promote the industry - b) Greater Victoria Bike to Work Society - $1,500 for Bike to Work Week c) Royal Canadian Legion - $2,500 for Remembrance Day luncheon; plus funding of $3,000 towards a Christmas Dinner 2018. d) Fort Rodd Hill and Fisgard Lighthouse - $1,500 for Canada Day celebration e) Your Literacy Connection - $500 to promote literacy in Langford f) Lighthouse Christian School - $1,000 for grad g) Goldstream Nature House \u2014 Chums sponsorship program $1,000 2. New Requests: h) Big Brothers Big Sisters of Victoria and Area -$1,000 for mentoring program i) M'Akola Housing Society - $1500 for Westshore Indigenous Festival Deny the following 2018 funding requests due to budgetary constraints: 1. New Requests: a) Royal Bay Secondary School Parent Grad Committee - $2,000 towards Dry Grad Carnival - Council direct staff to work with the school in 2019 to develop a similar agreement for fee for service as Belmont Secondary School. b) Lions Pride Gymnastics Society - $250 - $2,500 for sponsorship - Council requests that Lion's Pride do a presentation to the committee in 2019. c) Open Gate Church - Council may agree to $1500 in funding after further information on the Langford/Colwood Neighbourhood Free Fresh Food Market is provided by staff.",
